Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.89,0:00:05.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,The Puth thread didn't end with the\Ncover Two years later when the group
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.01,0:00:08.73,Cap,,0,0,0,,finally released its first album track\Nfour would be called Like That
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.23,0:00:13.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,written and gifted by Charlie Puth\Nhimself explicitly in response to that
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.85,0:00:18.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,practice-room video Remember the\Nsequence because it matters a cover
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.56,0:00:23.59,Cap,,0,0,0,,made in anonymity went up the chain\Nreached the original artist and came
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.48,0:00:28.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,back down as a song on a debut album\NIn an industry where Western features
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.94,0:00:32.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,are bought and negotiated one of the\Nbiggest pop writers on Earth handed a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.58,0:00:35.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,debut track to a trainee he had never\Nmet
